    "created_at": "2022-07-20T14:19:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-20T14:19:56Z",
    "body": "I don't know how web-interoperable including both max-age and no-cache on the same cache-control is.\r\n\r\nAll of this is assuming a non-cacheable resource (for the disk cache) and a resource that can only be used once.  If that part of Chrome's implementation is going to go away and it is going to behave like a normal cache resource then none of this is needed (but prefetching HTML also won't work in a lot of cases).\r\n\r\nstale-while-revalidate also assumes multiple uses of the response and would populate the disk cache (and presumably there is no \"real\" response if the request can be satisfied from the prefetched response).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
