    "updated_at": "2022-07-20T18:04:09Z",
    "body": "@pmeenan: seems like the main use-case for prefetch with `no-cache` is fetching documents. Would you say that's right? JS & CSS files that are the other mime-types used by prefetch are largely immutable or at least don't tend to change according to cookies etc.\r\n\r\nIf that's so, I think trying to solve this here has been done before and led to the current effort on nav-speculation. In a world where nav-speculation is mature, the place where prefetch \"shines\" is in early fetch of subsequent subresources (mainly styles & scripts). And for that case, fine-tuning for `no-cache` and the above cases are perhaps less relevant?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
